# Test: OSPFv2 SPF route installation.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-ospf-8-spf-rib -- hand-built OSPF LSDB input reaches the SPF
# route table and inserts one Loc-RIB path per OSPF next-hop with Source=ospf,
# admin distance 110, ECMP instances, sysrib ECMP membership updates, and
# withdraw on loss.
# PREVENTS: regressions that compute SPF but bypass the Loc-RIB install path,
# regressions where Loc-RIB suppresses ECMP membership-only updates before
# sysrib/fibkernel can see them, and OSPF ECMP collapsing to one next-hop.
#
# Live multi-node kernel assertions (remote prefix as RTPROT_ZE, ECMP multipath,
# and withdrawal after neighbor loss) require Linux raw sockets/veth and are
# owned by the OSPF FRR/QEMU interop scenarios in spec-ospf-13, matching the
# IS-IS SPF/RIB test split. `ospf-route-daemon.ci` covers the daemon wiring half.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=go test -v ./internal/plugins/ospf/spf ./internal/core/rib/locrib ./internal/component/sysrib -run TestOSPF(SPFRoute|InstallPath|SPFECMP)$|TestOnChangeDispatchesECMPMembershipChanges$|TestSysRIBConsumesLocRIBECMPMembership$|TestSysRIBReplaysLocRIBECMPMembership$ -count=1:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=TestOSPFSPFRoute
expect=stdout:contains=TestOSPFInstallPath
expect=stdout:contains=TestOSPFSPFECMP
expect=stdout:contains=TestOnChangeDispatchesECMPMembershipChanges
expect=stdout:contains=TestSysRIBConsumesLocRIBECMPMembership
expect=stdout:contains=TestSysRIBReplaysLocRIBECMPMembership
